{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context\nAn AST inventory finds 110 broad environment constructions under tests: 51 `dict(os.environ)`, 49 `{**os.environ, ...}`, and 10 `os.environ.copy()`. Seven decorated pytest fixtures are owned by sibling `dumbstruck-wonderful-xiphosuran`, leaving exactly 103 test-local/helper sites here. A real pytest runtime probe proved that when process startup raises, default long tracebacks render ordinary environment mappings through `subprocess.run`, `Popen`, and `_execute_child`, exposing early inherited values; short tracebacks do not. A late sentinel can be truncated, so absence without insertion-order control is not proof. Production and maintenance propagation remain excluded.\n\n## Approach rationale\nThe sibling fixtures could use allowlists after a 24-test minimal-environment proof. This population cannot share one allowlist: `_store_isolation.py` intentionally forwards the invoking pytest environment, and live Jira child probes intentionally forward environment-only credentials. The boundary therefore retains exact mappings while redacting only representation. Value wrappers such as Pydantic `SecretStr` are unsuitable because `subprocess` requires plain string keys and values. The existing file `tests/scripts/test_autodeploy_env_repr_security.py` is the authoritative prior contract; the new `tests/unit/test_subprocess_env_repr_security.py` is a distinct held-out oracle for this ticket.\n\n## Plan\n- Add a test-only mutable dict boundary whose representation redacts contents, whose mapping behavior preserves exact inherited child environments, whose `.copy()` preserves the boundary, and whose `with_overrides(...)` is the sanctioned type-preserving derivation path.\n- Route all 103 non-fixture broad constructions through that boundary; retain every key/value/order and per-test override so intentional ambient propagation remains unchanged.\n- Add a real nested-pytest startup-failure oracle using `tests/integration/test_init_fail_closed.py::_env`, with a first-position sentinel and short-trace negative control.\n- Add an AST repository-policy guard that skips the seven separately-owned decorated fixtures and rejects new raw broad mappings.\n- Make the guard reject both direct and locally-aliased boundary unwrapping through `dict(boundary)` or `{**boundary, ...}`; require `.copy()` or `with_overrides(...)` instead.\n\n## Test contract card\n- authoritative_contract: existing `tests/scripts/test_autodeploy_env_repr_security.py:13-45` establishes failure-output non-disclosure.\n- new_oracle: `tests/unit/test_subprocess_env_repr_security.py` exercises this ticket population.\n- trigger_preconditions: sentinel is first; a real subprocess startup fails before returning.\n- production_path: `_env` -> real `subprocess.run` -> pytest long traceback.\n- test_tier: nested real pytest + real subprocess; a pure repr unit test cannot cross pytest/stdlib rendering.\n- observable_postcondition: long and short captured output omit the sentinel; successful child receives the exact value.\n- negative_control: short traceback never renders the sentinel.\n- ci_gate: `make test` / unit repository-policy lane.\n\n## Testing\n- Run `pytest tests/unit/test_subprocess_env_repr_security.py -q` for the held-out oracle, successful-child contract, and AST guard.\n- Run `pytest` for affected consumers.\n- Run `make lint` and `make typecheck`.\n- Seed each raw constructor form, `dict(boundary)`, and `{**boundary}`; the guard must name every offender.\n- Replace the representative boundary with an ordinary dict; the security oracle must fail.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] `pytest tests/unit/test_subprocess_env_repr_security.py -q` proves zero unclassified raw mappings remain among the 103 inventoried sites.\n- [ ] The seven decorated fixtures are excluded structurally under the existing `discovered_from` link to `dumbstruck-wonderful-xiphosuran`.\n- [ ] The nested default-long traceback test omits a first-position sentinel.\n- [ ] The nested short traceback control omits the sentinel.\n- [ ] The successful-child test proves exact inherited values reach the child.\n- [ ] `pytest` preserves every intentional ambient-propagation behavior.\n- [ ] Seeded `dict(os.environ)`, `{**os.environ}`, and `os.environ.copy()` mutations make the guard name the offending location.\n- [ ] Seeded `dict(boundary)` direct and alias mutations make the guard name the offending location.\n- [ ] Seeded `{**boundary}` direct and alias mutations make the guard name the offending location.\n- [ ] `make lint` passes.\n- [ ] `make typecheck` passes.\n- [ ] Replacing the representative safe boundary with an ordinary dict returns the held-out security oracle to RED."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1787035044886179001,"uuid":"86cbb929-8bd1-4664-8dec-55194e8dc4bd"}